# Crawler Development Patterns

## URL Handling

```rust
use url::Url;

/// Normalize a URL for consistent storage and deduplication.
pub fn normalize_url(url: &Url) -> Url {
    let mut normalized = url.clone();

    // Lowercase host
    if let Some(host) = normalized.host_str() {
        // URL crate handles this automatically
    }

    // Remove default ports
    if normalized.port() == Some(80) && normalized.scheme() == "http" {
        normalized.set_port(None).ok();
    }
    if normalized.port() == Some(443) && normalized.scheme() == "https" {
        normalized.set_port(None).ok();
    }

    // Sort query parameters for consistency
    // Remove fragments (they're client-side)
    normalized.set_fragment(None);

    normalized
}
```

## Politeness / Rate Limiting

Always implement rate limiting:

```rust
use governor::{Quota, RateLimiter};
use std::num::NonZeroU32;

pub struct PolitenessEngine {
    global_limiter: RateLimiter<...>,
    per_domain: DashMap<String, RateLimiter<...>>,
}

impl PolitenessEngine {
    pub async fn wait_for_permission(&self, domain: &str) {
        // Global rate limit
        self.global_limiter.until_ready().await;

        // Per-domain rate limit
        let domain_limiter = self.per_domain
            .entry(domain.to_string())
            .or_insert_with(|| create_domain_limiter());

        domain_limiter.until_ready().await;
    }
}
```

## robots.txt Compliance

Always check robots.txt:

```rust
use robotstxt::Robots;

pub struct RobotsChecker {
    cache: DashMap<String, Robots>,
}

impl RobotsChecker {
    pub async fn is_allowed(&self, url: &Url) -> bool {
        let host = match url.host_str() {
            Some(h) => h,
            None => return false,
        };

        let robots = self.get_or_fetch_robots(host).await;
        robots.is_allowed(&self.user_agent, url.path())
    }
}
```

## Content Extraction

Use CSS selectors with the scraper crate:

```rust
use scraper::{Html, Selector};

pub fn extract_links(html: &str, base_url: &Url) -> Vec<Url> {
    let document = Html::parse_document(html);
    let selector = Selector::parse("a[href]").unwrap();

    document.select(&selector)
        .filter_map(|el| el.value().attr("href"))
        .filter_map(|href| base_url.join(href).ok())
        .filter(|url| url.scheme() == "http" || url.scheme() == "https")
        .collect()
}

pub fn extract_text(html: &str, selector: &str) -> Option<String> {
    let document = Html::parse_document(html);
    let sel = Selector::parse(selector).ok()?;

    document.select(&sel)
        .next()
        .map(|el| el.text().collect::<String>().trim().to_string())
}
```

## Retry Logic

Implement exponential backoff:

```rust
use std::time::Duration;
use tokio::time::sleep;

pub async fn fetch_with_retry<F, T, E>(
    mut operation: F,
    max_retries: u32,
) -> Result<T, E>
where
    F: FnMut() -> futures::future::BoxFuture<'static, Result<T, E>>,
{
    let mut attempt = 0;
    loop {
        match operation().await {
            Ok(result) => return Ok(result),
            Err(e) if attempt < max_retries => {
                attempt += 1;
                let delay = Duration::from_millis(100 * 2u64.pow(attempt));
                sleep(delay).await;
            }
            Err(e) => return Err(e),
        }
    }
}
```

